Implement a client-server application using sockets, 
whose functionality will be the transmission 
of a file from the server to the client.

The exercise will consist of two parts (processes):

The server. A process that will be waiting for connections to arrive from the client 
and, once the connection is established, 
will transfer to the client the contents of a file named "Google.html". 
The contents of the file will be the source code of Google's web page.


The client. A process that will establish the connection with the server, 
receive the contents of the file, and display it on screen.

The client will run on the local machine and will be invoked with the command:

Cliente IP_Servidor

The server will be launched with the command Server 
and must be listening at all times on port 9999, 
ready to accept connections. After a connection request from a client, 
it must create a child process that will be responsible 
for carrying out all the operations necessary for the file transfer.

